    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="30.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 30.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>And æt þam oðrum cyrre ne si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.6"/> þær nan oðer bót, gif he fúl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.21"/> wurðe, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.22"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man ceorfe him ða handa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.star"/> oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.23"/> þa fet oððe ægþer, be þam ðe seo dæd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.24"/> sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.6"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>And æt ðam oðran cyrre ne sy ðær nan oþer bot, buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.3"/> gyf he ful wurðe, buton ðæt man ceorfe him ða handa oððe ða fǽt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.4"/> óf oððe ægðer, be ðam ðe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>And æt þam oðrum cerrę ne sy þær nan oðor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.1"/> bot, gif he ful wurðe, buton þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man ceorfe him þa handa of oððe þa fet oððe ægðer, be þam þe seo dæde sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Ad secundam uicem non sit alia emendatio, si reus fuerit, nisi ut amputentur ei manus aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.12"/> pedes aut utrumque, secundum quod factum erit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Si secundo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.17"/> ceciderint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.18"/>, abscidantur illis manus aut pedes aut utrumque, si culpa tanta fuerit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.19"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi iterum tale facere presumpserit et Dei iudicio conuictus fuerit, nullam redempcionem habeat, quin ei truncentur manus aut pedes aut utrumque, iuxta quod peccati quantitas exegerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="30.4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="190" ed="#robertson"/>And æt ðam oðran cyrre ne sy ðær nan oþer bot, gyf<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_30-4.robnote.fn.8"/> he ful wurðe, buton ðæt man ceorfe him ða handa oððe ða fǽt óf oððe ægðer, be ðam ðe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="270" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And æt þam oðrum cyrre, ne si þær nan oðer bot gif he ful wurðe butan þæt man ceorfe him ða handa oððe þa fet oððe ægþer, be þam ðe seo dæd sig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn er zum zweiten Male schuldig befunden wird, gebe es keine andere Busse, als dass man ihm die Hände<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.de.1"/> oder die Füsse oder beides<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.de.2"/> abhaue<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_30-4.lnote.de.3"/>, je nachdem die That ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if he is found guilty the second time, let there be no other compensation than that his hands or his feet or both be cut off, according to what the deed is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-4.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="191" ed="#robertson"/>And on the second occasion, if he is proved guilty, there shall be no compensation possible to him but to have his hands or his feet cut off or both, according to the nature of the offence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="466" ed="#whitelock"/>And on the second occasion there is to be no other compensation, if he is convicted, but that his hands, or feet, or both, in proportion to the deed, are to be cut off.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="271" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if he is proven guilty a second time, there shall be no other possible compensation except to have his hands or feet cut off or both, according to the seriousness of the crime.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="333"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-6">I Atr 1.6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 1, 6</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>echoes</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-5">I Atr 1.5</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:5, 2, 4 (echoed by II Cn 30:3b,4, 32, 33)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>echoes</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_2">I Atr 2</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:5, 2, 4 (echoed by II Cn 30:3b,4, 32, 33)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>echoes</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_4">I Atr 4</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:5, 2, 4 (echoed by II Cn 30:3b,4, 32, 33)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">‘of’ should probably be supplied in G from the other MSS. Liebermann compares I Atr 1.6.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 333, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gif he: buton gif he B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ut'que <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ut'que Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vorweg aus folgender Zeile, zu streichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">anticipated from the following line; to be deleted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> fætt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from fætt</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. p. <hi rend="italic">doppelt, aber unterpunctirt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. p. written twice, but expunged by subscript dots R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fuerit <hi rend="italic">HkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fuerit HkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">full <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">full Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton þ. m. ceorf <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton þ. m. ceorf Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> of <hi rend="italic">aus übr.?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply of from the others?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">of oþþa ða fete <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">of oþþa ða fete Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dæde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dæde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">deinde <hi rend="italic">Cb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">deinde Cb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rit a. illi <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rit a. illi S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor</hi> tanta <hi rend="italic">nachgetragen Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">added later before tanta Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Cnut ersetzt Todesstrafe der Quelle durch Verstümmelung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4; Hand 11e; Fuss 6); <hi rend="italic">vgl. o</hi>. 2, 1⁸. 25²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnut replaces the death penalty of the source by mutilation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4; Hand 11e; Fuss 6); <hi rend="italic">cf. above</hi> 2, 1⁸. 25²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ine 37 hatte nur eine Hand <hi rend="spaced">oder</hi> einen Fuss abhauen lassen; ‘Hände’ 48, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ine 37 had ordered only one hand <hi rend="italic">or</hi> one foot to be cut off; ‘hands’ 48, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_30-4.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ceorfan</hi> heisst auch ‘<hi rend="spaced">ab</hi>hauen’, neben ‘hauen’; die Hinzufügung von <hi rend="italic">of</hi> in BA verdeutlicht nur; streiche <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. I 332 Sp. 1*. <hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. Ine 18⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">ceorfan</hi> also means ‘cut <hi rend="italic">off</hi>’, besides ‘cut’; the addition of <hi rend="italic">of</hi> in BA merely makes this clearer; delete <hi rend="italic">above</hi> I 332 col. 1*. <hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. Ine 18⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_30-4.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. I Atr. 1, 6. Here again as in 8, 1 (cf. III Atr. 8; 16; IV, 5, 4) Canute replaces capital punishment by maiming. With regard to the infliction of this type of punishment by Canute, see <hi rend="italic">Sax. Chr.</hi>, ann. 1014.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_30-4.robnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><label>gyf</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gif</hi> G, A, Ld; <hi rend="italic">buton gyf</hi> B.</seg></note>
      </div>
